fact WorkItem(id: "WI-174", description: some(value: "Replace dependents-count ordering in 'anthill-todo list' with chronological+topological mixed ordering. Today run_list (anthill-todo/src/main.rs:522-616) splits items into ready/blocked, sorts ready by transitive dependents count (most-unblocking first), and sorts blocked by id. Behavior to deliver: walk filtered items in chronological order (by id, since WI-NNN is sequential); for each item X not yet emitted, recursively emit X's still-unemitted dependencies first (topological/postorder), then X. Result is one global sequence where (a) each item appears after all its dependencies, and (b) the top-level cursor advances through items in chronological order, so the earliest WI anchors a topologically-ordered cluster of its deps just before it. Concretely: replace the count_transitive-sorting block with a postorder DFS over a chronologically-sorted item list, marking emitted to avoid duplicates and to short-circuit shared deps. Keep the ready-vs-blocked split (and the blocked section labelling) only if it still adds value — preferred shape is one merged list with [blocked] tags inline. Open question to resolve in the WI: whether closed (Delivered/Verified) deps should be skipped from the emitted list (probably yes — they're satisfied and don't need re-display) or shown as anchors. Acceptance: cargo-test green; eyeball-check 'anthill-todo list' output on the current ~65 open items shows the earliest open item appearing near the top with its open deps clustered immediately before it."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-06-14T08:36:32Z"))

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-174", author: "user", content: "Status grouping: keep the existing top-level grouping by status — Open first, then Claimed, then Delivered (Verified hidden by default like today). Within each status group, apply the chronological+topological ordering described above. So the output shape is: [Open group: chrono-walk with deps clustered] then [Claimed group: same] then [Delivered group: same].", at: "2026-05-04T10:49:34Z")

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-174", author: "user", content: "Keep the existing 'blocked' group as today: items with unmet deps go under a separate '-- blocked --' section. Apply chrono+topo ordering within both the ready section and the blocked section. So combined with status grouping: Open(ready: chrono+topo) / Open(blocked: chrono+topo) / Claimed(...) / Delivered(...).", at: "2026-05-04T10:50:04Z")

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-174", author: "user", content: "DELIVERED 2026-06-14. Reworked anthill-todo list ordering in the embedded bundle (anthill/main.anthill cmd_list_plain — the WI's native run_list ref was stale, ported at WI-009 cutover). Replaced the unblocks-count ready sort with: status grouping (Open/Claimed/Delivered/Verified/PreOpened/Rejected/Stale headers, lifecycle order via status_rank; grouping driven by statuses actually present so no row is dropped) over the kept ready/-- blocked -- split, each section ordered by chrono_topo (postorder DFS: walk rows by id, emit each row's in-section not-yet-emitted deps first so deps cluster immediately before their dependent). [unblocks N] kept display-only (not a sort key). Deleted ready_lt/merge_ready/sort_ready. Golden parity regenerated; full anthill-todo suite 66/0 green; eyeball acceptance confirmed (WI-280/WI-282 cluster before WI-278). /code-review (4 angles): dup-id collapse latent (add auto-assigns unique ids; the one historical WI-169 dup spans two statuses->two groups, both shown) + documented; Rejected/Stale rank gap fixed.", at: "2026-06-14T08:36:28Z")
